<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perak War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1875–1876</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Perak War was a conflict of 1875–1876 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and Malay chiefs of Perak. It began after the first British Resident, J. W. W. Birch, was killed at Pasir Salak in November 1875 in resentment at his interference in local affairs. British and Indian troops crushed the resistance; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> Lela and others were hanged, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Abdullah was exiled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a>, and British control of Perak was strengthened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perak-war.jpg" alt="Perak War" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C. R. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blue-jackets_and_marines_poling_the_British_expedition_up_the_Perak_river,_1876.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
